Package: pseudopost
Title: Pseudo-Posterior Uncertainty Adjustment for Composite and Pseudo-Likelihood Stan Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Hok Chio (Mark)", "Lai", , "marklhc@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Post-hoc covariance (sandwich) adjustment for Bayesian models fit to
    composite, pairwise, or otherwise pseudo-likelihood-based Stan models via
    'cmdstanr'. For such models the naive inverse-Hessian posterior covariance is
    generally miscalibrated; 'pseudopost' provides post-hoc covariance
    (infinitesimal jackknife / Godambe sandwich) adjustments targeting the
    robust covariance to improve scale and coverage. It implements
    (1) an analytic point Godambe sandwich (the 'CurvAdj' family),
    (2) a draw-based infinitesimal jackknife (IJ) target estimated from the
    MCMC draws -- both a fast regression-proxy variant and a literal
    per-observation score variant in the style of Shaby (2014)
    <doi:10.1080/10618600.2013.842174> -- and (3) a scalar magnitude
    (scale) adjustment. Adjustments are returned as corrected
    standard errors / credible intervals and as affine-transformed posterior draws.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/marklai/pseudopost
